{
  "id": "hicks-room",
  "name": "Hicks's room",
  "description": "Hicks's one room on Level 2 of the Ribbon, behind the plain grey door on the walkway, down where the stack barely sees daylight. Bare concrete patched with sheet metal, pipes and cable everywhere, a drip from one joint into a tin can. A cot under a barred window onto the girders of the level above, and across the gap a wall of small windows and a red neon shape. In the middle, his rig: a battered desk with an open deck wired into a tower of salvaged hardware, three small monitors of green code, sandalwood incense smoking in a cup. A hot plate, a kettle and a sink; a little TV on a crate that only shows static; a dented locker of jackets. The grey steel door out to the walkway, two deadbolts and a chain, a lantern on a hook beside it, and low in the wall by the cot a small steel hatch, the back way down into Old Town. He owns very little, and nothing he'd miss.",
